{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>When she profanes.</b> According to many, from the pattern of תחלה. In my opinion, it is from the root חלות (profanation), only it is from the heavy doubled stem, like לא יחל דברו. On both interpretations the word is of the doubled roots, only it is unusual. It is possible that החל too, and תחל, do not intermingle with the meaning of תחלה, because the vav has a kamatz katon, and likewise לבלתי החל." "<b>And the daughter of a priest.</b> If she profaned herself through harlotry, because she profaned her father's honor." "<b>By fire she shall be burned.</b> As a burnt offering. Or, a betrothed woman."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:11:40.178034833Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}